 "capsule": "Estonia restored its independence from the Soviet Union on 20 August 1991, and the constitution adopted by referendum in June 1992 reestablished the parliamentary Republic of Estonia under first president Lennart Meri. The country pursued rapid market reform and pioneering 'e-governance' digitization, joining NATO and the European Union in 2004 and the eurozone in 2011, and has since become a noted hub for digital public services and cybersecurity policy in northern Europe.",
